<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Unknown coordinates for collinear points</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(A({@A[1]@},\,{@A[2]@},\,{@A[3]@})\), \(B({@B[1]@},\,{@B[2]@},\,{@B[3]@})\) and \(C(s,\,{@c2@},\,t)\) are collinear, with \(\overrightarrow{AC} = k\,\overrightarrow{AB}\). Fractions are fine; type a fraction with a slash, for example 5/3.</p><div>(a) \(k =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><div>(b) \(s =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><div>(c) \(t =\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(\overrightarrow{AB} = {@cv3(d)@}\) and \(\overrightarrow{AC} = \begin{pmatrix} s - ({@A[1]@}) \\ \displaystyle{@c2-A[2]@} \\ t - ({@A[3]@}) \end{pmatrix}\).</p><p>(a) The y-components are both known: \({@c2-A[2]@} = k \times ({@d[2]@})\), so \(k = {@kk@}\).</p><p>(b) \(s = {@A[1]@} + k \times ({@d[1]@}) = {@sp@}\).</p><p>(c) \(t = {@A[3]@} + k \times ({@d[3]@}) = {@tq@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[cv3(v) := matrix([v[1]],[v[2]],[v[3]]);
/* Design: unknown coordinates of a point on a line through two points, without the line equation; k found first. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 4, Chapter 9, Exercise E, Q7. */
clist: [[[-1,-1,-4],[-3,-3,-2],-5,2],[[5,5,-2],[4,3,2],-1,3],[[-1,-1,-3],[3,3,-1],9,5/2],[[-2,3,-1],[-4,1,1],0,3/2],[[3,2,-3],[2,3,-4],0,-2],[[2,-3,5],[4,-7,4],-19,4],[[3,3,2],[1,-1,6],5,-1/2],[[2,-1,-1],[0,-3,3],-8,7/2],[[-3,1,-2],[-1,4,1],-8,-3],[[1,4,-4],[4,7,-7],9,5/3]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
A: clist[ix][1]; B: clist[ix][2]; c2: clist[ix][3]; kk: clist[ix][4];
d: B-A;
sp: A[1]+kk*d[1]; tq: A[3]+kk*d[3];
kinv: 1/kk; pd: kk*d[1]; pin: A[1]+kinv*d[1]; qd: kk*d[3]; qin: A[3]+kinv*d[3];
k1: kk+1/3; sft: A[1]+k1*d[1]; tft: A[3]+k1*d[3];
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>ix={@ix@}, k={@kk@}, s={@sp@}, t={@tq@}</text>
  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Vectors II: unknown coordinates for collinear points</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.6: Find the scalar k and two unknown coordinates of a point collinear with two given points in three dimensions.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question 7 in Exercise E of Chapter 9 of Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 4 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2005: the line equation replaced by AC = k AB, the scalar found first, new points and letters, randomised over a curated list, with named and follow-through feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
